ry\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years. On the middle of the grids, 2025 ended dry, with November to December at 61% of normal. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 43% of normal and May to June at 166%. All 7 grids had their driest year in 1953, at 65% to 67% of normal.</p>"}
